2022-03-13 Alexander Necheff <alex@necheff.net>
    * Set version to 0.6.0
    * Added dynupd-broker to reload managed zone.
    * Modified dynupd to request zone reloads through dynupd-broker rather than attempt to reload the zone itself.
        Due to the way nsd-control works, dynupd would have required root permissions to reload the zone directly. Fixed issue #77.
    * Corrected an untracked issue where the provided install script set executable permissions on the systemd service unit for dynupd.
    * Corrected untracked issue with README that referenced pre Go module path name for executing integration tests.
    * Updated integration test Dockerfile to use Debian 11.
    * Updated integration tests to improve automation. Fixed issue #70, #41, and #39.
    * Deprecated test/nsddynum/run.sh as this functionality is now covered by unit and Docker integration tests.
    * Removed gosec from build system, golangci-lint now handles this role. Fixed issue #81.
    * Added Ginkgo as a dependency for testing.
    * Enhanced unit test coverage.
    * Enhanced tested edge cases in the auth package. Fixed issue #59.
    * Updated vendored dependencies.
    * Corrected an untracked issue where printf-style format strings were not properly specified in dynupd.
    * Added -b/--broker option to dynupd for specifying the dynupd-broker communication URI. Fixed issue #78.
    * Modified dynupd-broker to execute nsd-control in a sub-shell rather than directly. Fixed issue #88.
    * Corrected an issue where dynupd would only print a generic message if editing the zonefile failed. Now the
        lower level error (e.g. file not found) message is printed too to aid diagnostics. Fixed issue #93.
    * Added discussion of dynupd-broker to the README file. Fixed issue #80.

